      "content": "Goblin intuition, I suppose, is just a figure of speech – it's like having a sixth sense that tells you when something's off, but in this case, it's more like having a basic understanding of electrical systems and AC unit components. \n\nTo be honest, without seeing the unit, it's a bit tricky to pinpoint the exact issue. However, I can give you some general guidance. The humming noise without spinning fan could be due to a few possible causes. \n\nOne possibility is a faulty capacitor, which is a common component in AC units. If the capacitor is malfunctioning, it can cause the humming noise, but it won't affect the fan's spinning. You can try to replace the capacitor, but be careful not to touch any electrical components.\n\nAnother possibility is a loose or corroded connection, which can also cause the humming noise. In this case, you might need to check the connections and tighten any loose screws or replace any corroded parts.\n\nBefore you start tinkering, make sure to shut off the power to the AC unit at the circuit breaker or fuse box. This will prevent any accidental shocks or electrical fires. It's always better to be safe than sorry, especially when dealing with electrical components.\n\nIf you",
